# The build context is ./backend, and MEDIA_DIR defaults to ./data/media —
# so an importer run started from backend/ leaves ~110MB of re-hosted images
# sitting inside the context. .gitignore keeps them out of git but Docker
# does not read .gitignore, so every build shipped all of it to the daemon
# for a binary that needs none of it.
data/

# Never let a credentials file reach the daemon. The Dockerfile copies only
# source and the final image is distroless, but the build context is what
# gets uploaded, cached, and surfaced in build logs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Deliberately NOT excluding *_test.go or testdata/. They cost almost
# nothing to transfer, and excluding them would mean a future `go test` step
# added to the Dockerfile silently compiles no tests and passes — the same
# quiet-success failure this file's first entry exists to avoid.
